.Trash/**
Applications/**
Library/**

# Chrome state: per-context browsing history, kept PLAINTEXT and LOCAL.
# This dotfiles repo is public (github.com/pcmariani/dotfiles), and these files
# hold real URLs from client work -- account ids, component UUIDs, ticket links.
# They reach the repo only via yadm's ENCRYPTED archive; see
# ~/.config/yadm/encrypt. Never commit the plaintext.
.local/state/context/chrome/**
# The retired pinned-tab store, same reasoning. Stage 3 deletes the feature.
.config/context/tabs/**

# Agent browser credentials. Same reasoning as the Chrome state above, and the
# same repo: these are SECRETS, not just private data. Both are mode 0600 and
# were untracked -- but `yadm status -uall` reports 432,640 untracked files in
# $HOME, so a single `yadm add -A` would have staged a GitHub token into a
# public repository. Nothing was exposed; this closes the door.
# Found 2026-09-10 while committing the workspace switcher.
.agent-browser/**
